Hi B12,
Bryan Balingit posted a new announcement in Ekonomiks 9-Einstein  
<https://classroom.google.com/c/MTkwMzY5NzI2MDA0>.

Greetings 9 Einstein!

For our 3rd Quarter, you guys will be in charge of our online class  
sessions - yep, you will be reporting as a group. Below is a PPT containing  
your groupings and the content of your report, as well as the Unit 3  
Learners Material (the book that we use as main reference - now in PDF).

FAQs:

Reporting will start the week after the lent, same day.
You will be given the entire allocated time we have for class when  
reporting.
Individual documentation (per student or group member) of your  
participation and contribution to your group is a MUST.
Make use of all the resources you have, may that be an incorporation of  
other info coming from other references into your report, It's the digital  
age and you're the captain.

BE RESOURCEFUL.
BE CREATIVE.
SURPRISE ME WITH YOUR IDEAS AND THE WAYS YOU CAN EXECUTE 'EM.

Use this maxim as a guide: "Without ever sacrificing the content of your  
report, as a student in the digital age, how would you learn best if you're  
the one making the call?"

Promise, kapag powerful ang kinalabasan ng inyong report WALA na tayong  
ibang gagawin - no more activities, no more quizzes.

Best of luck and see you! :)

GROUP #1 is the first one to report of course.
OPEN <https://classroom.google.com/c/MTkwMzY5NzI2MDA0/p/MzA3MjkyOTEyODg2>
If you don't want to receive emails from Classroom, you can unsubscribe  
<https://classroom.google.com/s>.

Google LLC
1600 Amphitheatre Pkwy
Mountain View, CA 94043 USA

